    "PREAMBLE": "Gurmukh Singh vs Harbans Singh And Another on 16\nDecember, 2023\nAuthor: Pankaj Jain\nBench: Pankaj Jain\nCrm-M No.63479 of 2023 (O&M) on oe 2023:Phhc:161787\n117\nIn The High Court Of Punjab And Haryana\nAt Chandigarh\nCrm-M No.63479 of 2023 (O&M)\nDate of decision : 16.12.2023\nGurmukh Singh\nvecene Petitioner\nversus\nHarbans Singh & anr.\neveee Respondents\nCoram : Hon'Ble Mr.Justice Pankaj Jain\nPresent :-\nRee\nMr. Tarun Singla, Advocate\nfor the petitioner.\nRee\nPankaj Jain, J. (Oral)\nLearned counsel for the petitioner though submits that the act was intentional but he has not been able to point out any falsity in the said report.\nGurmukh Singh vs Harbans Singh And Another on 16 December, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/184725825/\n2 7\n",
    "facts": "By way of present petition filed under Section 482 Cr.P.C.\npetitioner seeks modification/quashing of order dated 14.02.2023 (Annexure P-11) passed by SDJM Phul dismissing the complaint qua respondent No.1/accused No.4 in the complaint.\nRespondent No.1 was in office as Station House Officer.\nPetitioner moved an application 156(3) Cr.P.C. seeking registration of FIR against the accused.\nBoth are on bail.\nReport is submitted for appropriate orders.\n",
    "ANALYSIS": "From the conjoint reading of the aforesaid report as well as the order it is evident that SHO reported to the Court with respect to pending FIR, however, the same was mistook by the concerned Court as the report on the application believing that FIR already stands registered.\nIn view of aforesaid circumstances, this Court does not find any reason to interfere in the impugned order dated 14.02.2023 wherein the trial Court held that so far as respondent No.1/accused No.4 is concerned there was no evidence that he ever intentionally gave a false report in the Court.\n",
    "decision": "In view of above, the present petition is dismissed.\n"
